# Fewer Keystrokes: settings for a faster shell
#
# Write one setting under each comment, then save. To try the file, load it into your terminal:
#   source fast.bashrc
# Loading it lasts until the terminal closes. Your own ~/.bashrc stays as it is, unless you
# copy these lines into it yourself (back it up first).

# 1. Remember the last 10000 commands while a terminal is open.


# 2. Keep the last 20000 commands in the history file.


# 3. Add each terminal's commands to the history file instead of replacing it.


# 4. Save each command to the history file as soon as it has run.


# 5. Let ** reach into every folder below.


# 6. Let cd find the folders right inside photo-show from anywhere, after it looks in the folder
#    you're in. Use photo-show's full path (cd into it and run pwd to see it). Don't export it.
